{"study_accession":"PRJNA879720","secondary_study_accession":"SRP396768","title":"Propagated circulating tumor cells uncover the role of NF-kB and COP1 in metastasis","description":"Circulating tumor cells (CTCs), a population of cancer cells that represents the seeds of metastatic nodules, are a promising model system for studying metastasis. In this study, we perform NGS on cultured CTCs and corresponding CTC-derived xenografts for four different unique patients. Using RNA-sequencing and DNA-sequencing, we establish a prospective role for NF-kB signaling and COP1 muations in driving successful cancer metastasis. Overall design: Samples were drawn from healthy donors and patient-specific whole blood (WB), cultured CTCs (CTCs), and CTC-derived xenograft primary tumors (CDX tumors) and corresponding tissues with macrometastatic nodules.","pubmed":"36980717","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN30811724","study_accession":"PRJNA879720","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"HD 5","description":"HD 5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6573303","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-04-01","attributes":[["source_name","HD 5"],["source","Healthy Donor Blood"],["disease","Healthy Donor"],["tissue","Whole Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21533715","experiment_accession":"SRX17536067","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":82796727,"base_count":25004611554,"first_public":"2023-04-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6573303: HD 5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN30811728","study_accession":"PRJNA879720","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"HD 6","description":"HD 6","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6573299","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-04-01","attributes":[["source_name","HD 6"],["source","Healthy Donor Blo